      {
        "claim": "landmark_10_soft_mass is the cleanest observed contrast: 14 independent batches, only 2 strong sign conflicts, relative node RMSE 0.51, and a curve that rises from about -0.38 z at t=0 to a mid-window plateau near +0.8 z before declining to about -0.37 z at t=0.49.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "continuous:100",
          "curve_support"
        ],
        "id": "F004",
        "priority": 4
      },
      {
        "claim": "landmark_00_soft_mass shows the same rise-then-fall shape with 14 independent batches, 1 strong sign conflict and relative node RMSE 0.29, rising from about -0.37 z at t=0 to a peak near +1.6 z around t=0.16 and returning to about -0.28 z at t=0.49.",
        "evidence_ids": [
          "continuous:0",
          "curve_support"
        ],
        "id": "F005",
        "priority": 5
      },
      {
        "claim": "No polynomial was accepted for any landmark soft_mass curve (polynomial_accepted false, extrapolation_allowed false), so the observed window cannot be extended beyond [0.0, 0.49] and no absolute coordinate target or spatial gradient is specified by these contrasts.",
        "evidence_ids": [
